# Code owners — the paths that decide what the automation may do to itself.
#
# This repository is PUBLIC, accepts outside contributions, and runs an autonomous agent pipeline
# that opens and merges its own PRs. Everything below is a control surface: change one and you
# change what every later change is allowed to do. They require an explicit human approval; the
# rest of the tree does not, so routine agent work keeps merging unattended.
#
# Order matters — the LAST matching pattern wins, so the catch-all comes first.
#
# HONEST LIMIT, worth knowing before you rely on this: the agent pipeline authenticates as
# @gitchrisqueen, so GitHub cannot tell an agent PR from an owner PR. Against the agent, CODEOWNERS
# is therefore a speed bump and a paper trail, not a wall — the real control is the pipeline's
# credential having no `workflows` permission (docs/contribution-security.md). This file is the
# wall against OUTSIDE contributors, and it becomes a wall against the agent the moment the
# pipeline moves to its own bot identity.

*                                       @gitchrisqueen

# --- CI/CD and the rules themselves ---------------------------------------------------------
# A merged PR can currently rewrite any workflow, including the ones that gate merges and deploys.
/.github/                               @gitchrisqueen
/.github/workflows/                     @gitchrisqueen
/.github/CODEOWNERS                     @gitchrisqueen
/.github/actions/                       @gitchrisqueen
/.github/dependabot.yml                 @gitchrisqueen

# --- The autonomous pipeline ----------------------------------------------------------------
# tick.sh holds the trust boundary (who may hand work to an agent); RUNBOOK.md is the instruction
# set that agent reads. Both are self-modification surfaces.
/scripts/agent-pipeline/                @gitchrisqueen

# --- Anything that reaches production -------------------------------------------------------
/scripts/deploy.sh                      @gitchrisqueen
/scripts/rollback.sh                    @gitchrisqueen
/scripts/check_env.sh                   @gitchrisqueen
/scripts/vps_bootstrap.sh               @gitchrisqueen
/scripts/stack_watchdog.sh              @gitchrisqueen
/scripts/install_watchdog.sh            @gitchrisqueen
/scripts/backup.sh                      @gitchrisqueen
/scripts/systemd/                       @gitchrisqueen
/docker-compose.yml                     @gitchrisqueen
/docker-compose.prod.yml                @gitchrisqueen
/compose/local/Dockerfile               @gitchrisqueen
/.litellm/                              @gitchrisqueen

# --- Identity, sessions, secrets ------------------------------------------------------------
# `api/main.py` is the ONE place a caller is resolved (get_session_user_id / require_session_user_id
# / the scope surfaces), so an auth regression here is not local to one route.
/src/cqc_lem/api/main.py                @gitchrisqueen
/src/cqc_lem/utilities/auth_factors.py  @gitchrisqueen
/src/cqc_lem/utilities/auth_rate_limit.py @gitchrisqueen
/src/cqc_lem/utilities/webauthn_util.py @gitchrisqueen
/src/cqc_lem/utilities/crypto.py        @gitchrisqueen

# --- Schema ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Migrations are forward-only against live production data.
/compose/local/database/migrations/     @gitchrisqueen

